# What the image does not need, or must not hold. The paths are the ones of the build context, which is the root of the
# repository: `**/` is how a name is excluded at any depth.
#
# The server reads engine/, api/, ai/, web/, Data/, starter-kit/, benchmarks/ and docs/LIMITS*: all of them stay in.
# So does tests/: the "Assumptions & evidence" drawer re-runs the equality with the starter kit live, and what it runs is
# tests/test_vs_starter_kit.py, on the server itself. Without that folder the check would fail on the demo.

# The history, the environment of this machine and its caches.
.git
.github
.venv
.env
.env.*
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store

# Local reports: what the live commands and their dry runs write on a machine, and the coverage reports. None is
# part of what the server serves.
reports
benchmarks/*.tmp

# Not run by the server: the scripts that record answers, run the benchmark and make the picture, the pictures of the
# documents, and the files of this very configuration.
scripts
docs/screenshots
docs/demo.gif
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
render.yaml
